{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וישבע יוסף את בני ישראל", :translit "vayishba yosef et bnei yisrael", :gloss "And Joseph swore the children of Israel"} {:he "ולא השביע לבניו אלא אמר להם משכם לקחתם אותי ולשם תחזירוני", :translit "velo hishbia livnav ela amar lahem mishkam lakachtem oti ulesham tachziruni", :gloss "And he did not swear his sons but said to them: when He takes you up, take me with you, and to there return me"} {:he "ובמדרש יש שהשביעם שלא ידחקו את הקץ", :translit "uvamidrash yesh shehishbiam shelo yidcheku et haketz", :gloss "And in the Midrash there are those who say he swore them not to press the End"} {:he "כי יוסף ידע את הקץ שיעקב גלה לו", :translit "ki yosef yada et haketz sheya'akov gala lo", :gloss "for Joseph knew the End, which Jacob had revealed to him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Textual observation: verse says 'children of Israel' not 'his sons,' implying a broader oath to all the tribes."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'the children of Israel' rather than 'his sons' indicates Joseph addressed all Israel. Bereshit Rabbah 100:12 records that Joseph made his brothers swear they would carry his bones up from Egypt, but he did not impose the same oath on his own sons. The same Midrash source states that Jacob revealed the time of the End (keitz) to Joseph. The exhortation not to 'press the End' (lo yidcheku et haketz) is a known Talmudic concept found at Ketubot 111a and Sanhedrin 97b, where taking oaths not to force the redemption is discussed. The Ba'al HaTurim attributes the specific combination—that Joseph swore all Israel not to press the End because Jacob had revealed the keitz to him—to Midrashic tradition.", :sources ["Bereshit Rabbah 100:12" "Ketubot 111a" "Sanhedrin 97b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Textual observation: verse says 'children of Israel' not 'his sons,' implying a broader oath to all the tribes.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:12:48.543007762Z", :model "glm-5.2"}